{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543815-time","id":1543815,"title":"Time?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-14T19:56:55-07:00","id":1543815,"title":"Time?","content":"In Requiem-games, time can be a factor; how do you deal with time? That is, have their been any games that took advantage of one asset a vampire has? Did your ST use that fact in the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T02:59:13-07:00","id":1543849,"title":"","content":"Can you provide more context to your question? <br /> Time passes. In my games, if nothing very pressing is happening, I am one session to be one week of in game time, that way, the time moves forward alongside the weekly games. If something urgent is happening, I might do nightly, but would then do a bigger time skip after the story to give the in-universe time some mobility, and to avoid neonate PCs becoming elder level threats over a course of a few in game months. <br /> <br /> What do you mean by an asset? Plenty of merits are assets which have been used by characters in my games. As well as assets out there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T17:09:46-07:00","id":1543927,"title":"","content":"I suspect this is about vampires being immortal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T20:14:50-07:00","id":1544338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543815-time?p=1543849#post1543849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you provide more context to your question?<br /> Time passes. In my games, if nothing very pressing is happening, I am one session to be one week of in game time, that way, the time moves forward alongside the weekly games. If something urgent is happening, I might do nightly, but would then do a bigger time skip after the story to give the in-universe time some mobility, and to avoid neonate PCs becoming elder level threats over a course of a few in game months.<br /> <br /> What do you mean by an asset? Plenty of merits are assets which have been used by characters in my games. As well as assets out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry; meaning that, since vampires are immortal, days. months, years and even decades can pass in game-time. Players are not necessarily bound by the old RPGing, &quot;What are you doing today(Night)&quot;, question, night-by-night. <br /> <br /> In the Dark Ages, I used the Campaign-cartographer to build a medieval-town, and, I had time pass, a century, and I turned the thatch-roofs into tile-roofs, on the buildings, to simulate town-growth and change. It was literally uneventful, each night, for 100-years. Churches were built and the town grew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T20:33:16-07:00","id":1544769,"title":"","content":"One topic, a bit; so vampires, are literally asleep, for half of the day that is, on average, twelve-hours. Mortals, on the other hand, are awake sixteen to eighteen-hours a day; that makes mortals, more efficient with their time and, if you do the math, a 100 year-old vampire as only been conscience for 50-years of their life whereas a 100 year-old, mortal, 66 to 75 years, That would make the mortal, more mature than the ancilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T22:39:01-07:00","id":1544777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543815-time?p=1544769#post1544769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would make the mortal, more mature than the ancilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depands on how <b>VtR</b> points emotions and emotional adulthood. It easily could be that in the Embrace, you become your stable self. In the end, Embrace is the moment of your literal death.<br /> ) I;s reverse in the <b>Vampire Chronicles</b> of Ann Rice - <i><b><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=f331bfbc6967d90b&amp;rlz=1C1GCEB_enPL1123PL1123&amp;sxsrf=ADLYWIJVNzsiT84GSDxe-N7dpl6mu-7NPA:172